"Atop a Rotten Ladder"
"A layer of mildewy dampness covers the cool, natural ceiling above your head.

Rocky walls worn smooth by a constant trickle of water ripple downward into

darkness.  Moss clings to the ceiling, shifting occasionally as water sifts

through.  A rickety ladder, damaged by rot and decay, is attached to the wall

with iron bolts and descends into the pit below.

