#24752
"The Throne Room"
"The smooth, water-worn walls of the chamber blend with stone construction as

they near the floor.  A heavy, damp rug covers most of the cobble-stone floor,

stopping short of arched doorways in each direction.  The arches are rounded,

with heavy keystones of a lighter colored rock than the rest of the arch

holding them up.  Dominating the entire chamber is a large, granite throne

covered in a thin layer of fungus and moss.  A carving of a large troll can be

seen etched into the back.  From the flickering light given off by the torches

on the walls, you can make out rooms in all directions and an old, rotten

ladder just barely within arm's reach above you.

"
