#24754
"The Kitchen"
"The smell of soup fills the air of this narrow alcove.  A massive cast-iron

cauldron hangs above a small fire and fills the chamber.  Pressed up against

the southern wall is a small cot made of grubby canvas.  The cobblestone floor

is somewhat lean, with piles of dirt and mud swept into the corners.  The

walls, adorned only by torch-filled sconces, are somewhat dry.  The sloped

ceiling of the small room rises to the west and meets an archway.  Through the

arch you can see what appears to be a throne room.

"
""
